From tru64-unix-managers  Sat Feb 28 03:39:25 1998
From: Matt Groener <mwg () qad ! com>
Date: Sat, 28 Feb 1998 03:39:25 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY]: Monitor Resolution Changing in X/CDE
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078694111663


Thanks to all with helpful information. I apologize to those who tried to
help with what little technical information I provided.

The general consensus is to evaluate features in the "Xservers" file to
specify a screen resolution. The Xdec man page has all the features I
needed to know, including "-screenN" and "-syncN".

In addition, the video card needs to be considered in determining the
appropriate resolution options. In our case, we have an AlphaServer 2000
5/300, which has a very utilitarian video card. This card (ATI Mach64 GX)
is meant for functionality, not for multiple resolutions. Since this is a
workhorse server, the video card is really only meant to provide console
features.

I once again thank those who contributed to this discovery.

