From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Feb 26 17:11:22 1998
From: Alessandro Brunengo <root () infnux ! ge ! infn ! it>
Date: Thu, 26 Feb 1998 17:11:22 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Why adduser script doesn't update /etc/group anymore?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078694111615

Thanks for very fast responses to:
George Guethlein, Spider Boardman, Matt Moore and Declan Lennon

The answer is:

Adding a user's primary group information to /etc/group
merely created long lines there which could cause problems with
editors or even simply with attempts to parse the entries.  Since
the primary group information is taken from /etc/passwd anyway,
the duplication in /etc/group was merely redundant clutter, and
thus was removed.

More (from Declan):
... but as you will note
from the man page for adduser, the recommended utility for this purpose
is now useradd (or dxaccounts).

Thanks again.

Alessandro

On Wed, 25 Feb 1998, Alessandro Brunengo wrote:

