...
> Anyway, to change the behavior on file generation, add line:
>     sys_v_mode        1
> to your /usr/sys/conf/<SYSTEM> file and rebuild the kernel.
>
>No need to rebuild your kernel.  The system provides two approaches
>to enabling the sysV behavior:
>
>1) To enable sysV behavior system-wide, set "sys-v-mode = 1" in your
>   sysconfigtab file under the vfs stanza.
>
>2) To enable sysV behavior for a specific filesystem only, mount the
>   filesystem with the nogrpid option.

So there you have it. Number of ways to achieve the same things when you
really dig into it.

