With many thanks to rjackson@portal.gmu.edu, Here is a fix. I've applied
this to 20+ workstations here with immediate benefit.

DEC-droids: please see if you can get this added to sysconfigtab...

kdbx is on the optional s/w cd-rom and can be run as a standalone binary
so you only need to do the setld on server, and then run as root as required.

	-George


> The workaround is to patch the kernel as follows on your clients...
> 
> . kdbx -k /vmunix /dev/mem
> . (kdbx) patch do_client_readdirplus=0
> . (kdbx) quit
> 
> You can safely do this on a running system.  Unfortunately, Digital has not
> setup a sysconfigtab or /sys/conf/KERNEL method to date.  Let me know
> how it goes.  You will notice the benefit immediately and must do this 
> every time you build a new kernel.  Perhaps if enough users need this Digital
> Engineering will add something to sysconfigtab or /sys/conf/KERNEL.

