From: Boddy Bill NTSE <Bill.Boddy () nts ! hl ! siemens ! de>
Date: Tue, 10 Feb 1998 14:09:06 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY  volwatch
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078694111228


 
> 
> Has anyone out there managed to get volwatch  to send mail to a smtp
> address.
> 
> #man volwatch and the manuals aren't very helpful. 
> 
> Apparently volwatch will send any LSM errors to a mail user using
mailx.
> 
> 
> I have tried ..
> 
> 
> # volwatch bill.boddy@nts.hl.siemens.de   and it just hangs.  It also
> hangs if you type
> # volwatch root
> 
> Cheers
> 
> 
> Bill Boddy
Hi,
I've done it.  You have to modify two files: /etc/rc.config and
/sbin/init.d/lsm
1)	add the following lines to /etc/rc.config:

LSMNOTIFYID="root,user@host"
export LSMNOTIFYID

2)	make the following modifications to /sbin/init.d/lsm:

After the export PATH line at the start of the file add:
USER_ID='rcmgr get LSMNOTIFYID root'
and change the line:
/usr/sbin/volwatch &
to:
