Many thanks to George W. Baltz and Dr. Tom Blinn for their suggestions
which encouraged me to experiment further.

The answer was in the Release Notes (oops should have read these 1st!)
4.0D includes a secure version of syslog.
Remote logging hosts need to be added to the /etc/syslog.auth file
(mode 0600).

Once I'd created this file and added an entry for the Netblazer, all
was well.

Thanks,

