I asked for some reason why adduser made a new directory <username>
under /usr by default. 
I solved the problem myself just after sending the email - because
adduser is a shell script 
which have a look at /usr/users. If it doesn't exist (and it doesn't
exist after a 4.0D installation)
it recomment the /usr/<username> as the home directory. 

Dr. Tom Blinn, 603-884-0646 [tpb@zk3.dec.com] replied that he can't find
who made the change
and why, nor it's documented at the release notes. 

So simply make a /usr/users and all seems working as years before with
the adduser script.

best regards Dirk 

