From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Feb 03 09:55:01 1998
From: "Bryan G. Peterson" <peterson () physc1 ! byu ! edu>
Date: Tue, 03 Feb 1998 09:55:01 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Audio CD player for DU 3.2C (or 4.0B)
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078694111056

I'm sorry that I took so long to get this back - we are in the middle of a move 
between buildings and many things got pushed into the background for that move. 
Anyway, I asked about a cd player for DU 3.2C.  I got many responses that were 
very useful.  I took the "lazy" way out and used the one that is already on DU. 
It turned out that it wasn't precompiled but took about 5 minutes to find, 
recompile, and make work.  The sources were in /usr/examples/motif/xcd.  I 
apparently didn't install the X11 demos when I installed the OS so the 
precompiled version wasn't on the system.  One note was that I had to change 
the protections on the cd device - if I remember right I had to change the raw 
device (/dev/rrz6c) and the cam device (/dev/cam) - adding rw permission for 
the world.  I may be wrong on the cam device but I'm sure I did change the raw 
CD device.

I was in a bit of a hurry so I didn't get to try xmcd yet.

My thanks to the following for their input:

Steve VanDevender (stevev@hexadedimal.uoregon.edu)
Pat Lampert (lampert@decatl.alf.dec.com)
Paul A. Sand (pas@unh.edu)
Tom Webster (webster@ssdpdc.lgb.cal.boeing.com)
Don Becker (becker@panther.adelphi.edu)
George W. Baltz (gwb@umd5.umd.edu)
Martin Mokrejs (mmokrejs@mail.natur.cuni.cz)
John Becker (John.Becker@digital.com)
Akihito 'ycos' Yakoshi (yakoshi@osa.dec.com)
Lewis L. Lasser (lewis@dmi.stevens-tech.edu)
Simon Smith (sgs@his.com)

Summary:

1:  try xmcd (works on both DU 3.2 and 4.0) - get from
ftp://ftp.x.org/contrib/applications/xmcd/xmcd-2.2.tar.gz
ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/X11/R6-contrib/applications/xmcd/xmcd-2.2.tar.gz
http://sunsite.unc.edu/~cddb/xmcd/

2:  try xcd - binaries in /usr/bin/X11/demos/xcd or sources in 
/usr/examples/motif/xcd.  (Install OSFXDEMOS4xx or OSFXEXAMPLES4xx - it is also 
in the corresponding 3.2C installation))

3:  Try the scu(8) utility and the "play" subcommand or /sbin/scu
	Scu> help play

Thanks again (somewhat belatedly) for all your help.

Bryan Peterson
peterson@physc1.byu.edu

