From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Feb 03 08:10:38 1998
From: "Geert.VAN DEN EEDE" () SCIC ! cec ! be
Date: Tue, 03 Feb 1998 08:10:38 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Follow-up: Problem adding default route
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078694111042

Yesterday I sent this question to the list:

>>>>>
I have an Alpha 2000 that I recently upgraded to DU 4.0B (patch kit 5 installed). My machine reboots once a week on Sunday morning via cron. Ever since the upgrade the default route is not added automatically.
To find out the cause, I added some debugging information in /sbin/rc3 and in /sbin/rc3.d/S12route and had my machine rebooting every night. Since then the problem doesn't reoccur. 
On Friday I removed the debugging and this morning again the default route was not present.

Has anyone already seen this ? It seems like a timing problem. So far I have only seen this on 2 out of our 8 machines.

<<<<<

A lot of people replied me to check the contents of /etc/routes. Well there is nothing wrong with this file. If I add some debugging information in /sbin/rc3 and in /sbin/rc3.d/S12route, then the default route which is in /etc/routes is added fine.

One person replied me he was experiencing the same problem after applying patch kit 5 and even 6. So I am convinced that something is wrong. This morning the problem occured on a third machine.

Thanks for any help.



Geert Van den Eede
European Commission
Brussels - Belgium
e-mail: geert.vandeneede@scic.cec.be

